hadiths[188]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3761","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""The oath by which the Messenger of Allah used to swear was: 'No"
"3762","It was narrated from Salim that his father said:""The oath by which the Messenger of Allah used to swear was: 'No"
"3763","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:""When Allah created Paradise and Hell"
"3764","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears"
"3765","Yahya bin Abi Ishaq said:""A man from Banu Ghifar told me"
"3766","It was narrated from Salim"
"3767","It was narrated from 'Umar that the Prophet said:""Allah forbids you to swear by your forefathers."" 'Umar said: ""By Allah"
"3768","It was narrated from Salim"
"3769","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Do not swear by your fathers"
"3770","It was narrated that Thabit bin Ad-Dahhak said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam"
"3771","Thabit bin Ad-Dahhak narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:""Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam"
"3772","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Buraidah that his father said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever says: I have nothing to do with Islam"
"3773","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Yasar"
"3774","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah that the Prophet said:""Do not swear by your forefathers or by false gods (At-Tawaghit)"
"3775","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever among you swears and says: By Al-Lat"
"3776","It was narrated from Mus'ab bin Sa'd that his father said:""We were talking about something"
"3777","Mus'ab bin Sa'd narrated that his father said:""I swore by Al-Lat and Al-'Uzza and my companions said to me: 'What a bad thing you have said! You have said something horrible.' So I went to the Messenger of Allah and told him about that. He said: 'Say: La ilaha illallah wahdahu la sharika lah"
"3778","Al-Bara' bin 'Azib said:""The Messenger of Allah commanded us to do seven things: He commanded us to attend funerals"
"3779","It was narrated from Abu Musa that the Prophet said:""There is nothing on Earth that I swear an oath upon"
"3780","It was narrated that Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari said:""I came to the Messenger of Allah with a group of the Ash'ari people and asked him to give us animals to ride. He said: 'By Allah"
"3781","Amr bin Shu'aib narrated from his father"
"3782","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah that the Messenger of Allah said:""If any one of you swears an oath"
"3783","Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'If you swear an oath"
"3784","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah that the Prophet said:""If you swear an oath"
"3785","It was narrated that 'Adiyy bin Hatim said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath"
"3786","It was narrated that 'Adiyy bin Hatim said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath"
"3787","It was narrated that 'Adiyy bin Hatim said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath"
"3788","It was narrated from Abu Al-Ahwas that his father said:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"3789","It was narrated that 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah said:""The Prophet said to me: 'If you swear an oath"
"3790","Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'If you swear an oath"
"3791","Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah said:""The Messenger of Allah said to me: 'If you swear an oath"
"3792","Amr bin Shu'aib narrated from his father"
"3793","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Prophet said:""Whoever swears an oath and says: 'If Allah wills'"
"3794","It was narrated from 'Umar bin Al-Khattab that the Prophet said:""Actions are but by intentions"
"3795","Ubaid bin 'Umair said:I heard 'Aishah say: ""The Prophet used to stay with Zainab bint Jahsh and drink honey at her house. Hafsah and I agreed that if the Prophet came to either of us"
"3796","It was narrated that Jabir said:""I entered the house of the Prophet with him and there was some bread and vinegar. The Messenger of Allah said: 'Eat; what a good condiment is vinegar"
"3797","It was narrated that Qais bin Abi Gharazah said:""At the time of the Messenger of Allah we used to be called Samasir (brokers). The Messenger of Allah came to us when we were selling and called us by a name that was better than that. He said: 'O merchants (Tujjar)"
"3798","It was narrated that Qais bin Abi Gharazah said:""We used to sell in Al-Baqi"
"3799","It was narrated that Qais bin Abi Gharazah said:""The Prophet came to us when we were in the marketplace and said: 'This marketplace is filled with idle talk and (false) oaths"
"3800","It was narrated that Qais bin Abi Gharazah said:""In Al-Madinah we used to buy and sell Wasqs (of goods)"
"3801","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah forbade vows and said:""They do not bring any good; they are just a means of taking wealth from the miserly"
"3802","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah forbade vows and said: 'They do not change anything; they are just a means of taking wealth from the miserly"
"3803","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'A vow does not bring anything forward or put it back; it is just a means of taking wealth from the miserly"
"3804","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:""A vow does not bring anything to the son of Adam that has not been decreed for him. It is just a means of taking wealth from the miserly"
"3805","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet said:""Do not make vows"
"3806","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:""Whoever vows to obey Allah"
"3807","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'Whoever vows to obey Allah"
"3808","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'Whoever vows to obey Allah"
"3809","Imran bin Husain said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'The best of you are my generation"
"3810","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah passed by a man who was leading another man by a rope. The Prophet took it"
"3811","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet passed by a man who was circumambulating the Ka'bah"
"3812","It was narrated from 'Imran bin Husain that the Prophet said:""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"
"3813","It was narrated from Thabit bin Ad-Dahhak"
"3814","It was narrated that 'Uqbah bin 'Amir said:""My sister vowed to walk to the House of Allah"
"3815","Uqbah bin 'Amir narrated that he asked the Prophet about a sister of his who had vowed to walk"
"3816","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""A woman traveled by sea and vowed to fast for a month"
"3817","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that Sa'd bin 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah about a vow which his mother had sworn"
"3818","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""Sa'd bin 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah about a vow which his mother had sworn"
"3819","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""Sa'd bin 'Ubadah came to the Prophet and said: 'My mother died and she had sworn a vow"
"3820","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar"
"3821","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""Umar had made a vow to spend a night in 'Itikaf in Al-Masjid Al-Haram. He asked the Messenger of Allah about that"
"3822","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that 'Umar had vowed -during the Jahiliyyah- to spend a day in 'Itikaf. He asked the Messenger of Allah about that"
"3823","Abdullah bin Ka'b bin Malik narrated from his father"
"3824","Abdur-Rahman bin Ka'b bin Malik narrated that 'Abdullah bin Ka'b said:""I heard Ka'b bin Malik narrating his Hadith about when he stayed behind and did not join the Messenger of Allah on the campaign to Tabuk. He said: 'When I sat down before him I said: ""O Messenger of Allah"
"3825","Abdullah bin Ka'b bin Malik said:""I heard Ka'b bin Malik narrating his Hadith about when he stayed behind and did not join the Messenger of Allah on the campaign to Tabuk. (he said) I said: 'As part of my repentance I want to give my wealth in charity for Allah and His Messenger.' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Keep some of your wealth for yourself; that is better for you.' I said: 'I will keep for myself my share that is in Khaibar"
"3826","It was narrated from 'Ubaydullah bin Ka'b:""I heard my father Ka'b bin Malik narrate: 'I said: O Messenger of Allah"
"3827","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""We were with the Messenger of Allah in the year of Khaibar"
"3828","Abdullah bin 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills"
"3829","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills"
"3830","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah said:""Whoever swears an oath and says"
"3831","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:""Sulaiman bin Dawud said: 'Tonight I will go around ninety women"
"3832","It was narrated from 'Uqbah bin 'Amir that the Messenger of Allah said:""The expiation for vows is the expiation for an oath"
"3833","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"
"3834","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience and its expiation is the expiation for an oath"
"3835","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"
"3836","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"
"3837","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"
"3838","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"
"3839","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"
"3840","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience"
"3841","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain"
"3842","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath"
"3843","It was narrated that 'Imran said:The Messenger of Allah said: ""There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath"
"3844","It was narrated that 'Imran said:The Messenger of Allah said: ""There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath."" It was said: ""Az-Zubair did not hear this Hadith from 'Imran bin Husain"
"3845","It was narrated from Muhammad bin Az-Zubair"
"3846","It was narrated that Muhammad bin Az-Zubayr Hanzali said:My father told me that a man told him"
"3847","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:The Messenger of Allah said: ""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or at the time of anger"
"3848","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:The Messenger of Allah said: ""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience and its expiation is the expiation for an oath."" Mansur bin Zadhan contradicted him in his wording"
"3849","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:The Messenger of Allah said: ""There is no vow for the son of Adam with regard to that which he does not possess"
"3850","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah that the Prophet said:""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or with regard to that which the son of Adam does not possess"
"3851","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:The Messenger of Allah said: ""There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or with regard to that which the son of Adam does not possess"
"3852","It was narrated that Anas said:""The Prophet saw a man being supported by two others and said: 'What is this?' They said: 'He vowed to walk to the House of Allah.' He said: 'Allah has no need for this man to torture himself. Tell him to ride"
"3853","It was narrated that Anas said:""The Messenger of Allah passed by an old man who was being supported between two men and said: 'What is the matter with him?' They said: 'He vowed to walk.' He said: 'Allah has no need for him to torture himself. Tell him to ride.'"" So he was told to ride"
"3854","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""The Messenger of Allah came to a man who was being supported by two others and said: 'What is the matter with him?' It was said: 'He vowed to walk to the Ka'bah.' He said: 'Allah does not benefit from his torturing himself.' And he told him to ride"
"3855","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says: ""If Allah wills"
"3856","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah"
"3857","It was narrated from 'Ubaydullah bin Ka'b:\n I heard my father Ka'b bin Malik narrate: 'I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, has saved me by my being truthful, and as part of my repentance I want to give my wealth in charity to Allah and His Messenger. He said: Keep some of your wealth for yourself; that is better for you. I said: I will keep my share that is in Khaibar.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3857 Arabic Hadees: 3857"
"3858","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\n We were with the Messenger of Allah in the year of Khaibar, and we did not get any spoils of war except for wealth, goods and clothes. Then a man from Banu Ad-Dubaib, who was called Rifa'ah bin Zaid, gave the Messenger of Allah a black slave who was called Mid'am. The Messenger of Allah set out for Wadi Al-Qura. When we were in Wadi Al-Qura, while Mid'am was unloading the luggage of the Messenger of Allah, an arrow came and killed him. The people said: 'Congratulations! You will go to Paradise,' but the Messenger of Allah said: 'No, by the One in Whose hand is my soul! The cloak that he took from the spoils of war on the Day of Khaibar is burning him with fire.' When the people heard that, a man brought one or two shoelaces to the Messenger of Allah and the Messenger of Allah said: 'One or two shoelaces of fire.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3858 Arabic Hadees: 3858"
"3859","Abdullah bin 'Umar said:\n The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills, then he has made an exception.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3859 Arabic Hadees: 3859"
"3860","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\n The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills, then he has made an exception.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3860 Arabic Hadees: 3860"
"3861","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah said:\n Whoever swears an oath and says, 'If Allah wills,' then he has the choice: If he wishes, he may go ahead, and if he wishes he may not. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3861 Arabic Hadees: 3861"
"3862","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\n Sulaiman bin Dawud said: 'Tonight I will go around ninety women, each of whom will bear a horseman who will perform Jihad in the cause of Allah.' His companion said to him: 'If Allah wills.' But he did not say: 'If Allah wills.' Then he went around to them all, but none of them got pregnant except a woman who bore half a man. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! If he had said, 'If Allah wills,' they would all have performed Jihad in the cause of Allah as horsemen. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3862 Arabic Hadees: 3862"
"3863","It was narrated from 'Uqbah bin 'Amir that the Messenger of Allah said:\n The expiation for vows is the expiation for an oath. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3863 Arabic Hadees: 3863"
"3864","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3864 Arabic Hadees: 3864"
"3865","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\n There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3865 Arabic Hadees: 3865"
"3866","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3866 Arabic Hadees: 3866"
"3867","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\n There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3867 Arabic Hadees: 3867"
"3868","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3868 Arabic Hadees: 3868"
"3869","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\n There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3869 Arabic Hadees: 3869"
"3870","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\n There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3870 Arabic Hadees: 3870"
"3871","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:\n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3871 Arabic Hadees: 3871"
"3872","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain, may Allah be pleased with him, said:\n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3872 Arabic Hadees: 3872"
"3873","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:\n The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3873 Arabic Hadees: 3873"
"3874","It was narrated that 'Imran said:\nThe Messenger of Allah said:  There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3874 Arabic Hadees: 3874"
"3875","It was narrated that 'Imran said:\nThe Messenger of Allah said:  There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.  It was said:  Az-Zubair did not hear this Hadith from 'Imran bin Husain. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3875 Arabic Hadees: 3875"
"3876","It was narrated from Muhammad bin Az-Zubair, from his father, from a man from the inhabitants of Al-Basrah, who said:\n I accompanied 'Imran bin Husain, who said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah say: Vows are of two types: A vow that is made to do an act of obedience to Allah; that is for Allah and must be fulfilled, and a vow that is made to do an act of disobedience to Allah; that is for Shaitan and should not be fulfilled, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3876 Arabic Hadees: 3876"
"3877","It was narrated that Muhammad bin Az-Zubayr Hanzali said:\nMy father told me that a man told him, that he asked 'Imran bin Husain about a man who made a vow not to attend the prayers in the mosque of his people. 'Imran said: I heard the Messenger of Allah say: There is no vow at a moment of anger and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3877 Arabic Hadees: 3877"
"3878","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:\nThe Messenger of Allah said:  There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or at the time of anger, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3878 Arabic Hadees: 3878"
"3879","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:\nThe Messenger of Allah said:  There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.  Mansur bin Zadhan contradicted him in his wording. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3879 Arabic Hadees: 3879"
"3880","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:\nThe Messenger of Allah said:  There is no vow for the son of Adam with regard to that which he does not possess, or to do an act of disobedience to Allah, the Mighty and Sublime.  'Ali bin Zaid contradicted him -for he reported it from Al-Hasan from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3880 Arabic Hadees: 3880"
"3881","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah that the Prophet said:\n There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or with regard to that which the son of Adam does not possess. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3881 Arabic Hadees: 3881"
"3882","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:\nThe Messenger of Allah said:  There is no vow to commit an act of disobedience or with regard to that which the son of Adam does not possess. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3882 Arabic Hadees: 3882"
"3883","It was narrated that Anas said:\n The Prophet saw a man being supported by two others and said: 'What is this?' They said: 'He vowed to walk to the House of Allah.' He said: 'Allah has no need for this man to torture himself. Tell him to ride.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3883 Arabic Hadees: 3883"
"3884","It was narrated that Anas said:\n The Messenger of Allah passed by an old man who was being supported between two men and said: 'What is the matter with him?' They said: 'He vowed to walk.' He said: 'Allah has no need for him to torture himself. Tell him to ride.'  So he was told to ride. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3884 Arabic Hadees: 3884"
"3885","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:\n The Messenger of Allah came to a man who was being supported by two others and said: 'What is the matter with him?' It was said: 'He vowed to walk to the Ka'bah.' He said: 'Allah does not benefit from his torturing himself.' And he told him to ride. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3885 Arabic Hadees: 3885"
"3886","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\n The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever swears an oath and says:  If Allah wills, then he has made an exception. ' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3886 Arabic Hadees: 3886"
"3887","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah, who attributed it to the Prophet:\n Sulaiman said: 'I will certainly go around to ninety women tonight, each of whom will bear a child who will fight in the cause of Allah.' It was said to him: 'Say: If Allah wills' but he did not say it. He went around to them but none of them bore a child except for one woman who bore half a person.  The Messenger of Allah said:  If he had said: 'If Allah wills,' he would not have broken his vow, and this would have been a means to help him to get what he wanted. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3887 Arabic Hadees: 3887"
"3888","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed said:\n When you hire a worker, tell him what his wages will be. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3888 Arabic Hadees: 3888"
"3889","It was narrated from Al-Hasan that he disliked to hire a man without telling him what his wages would be. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3889 Arabic Hadees: 3889"
"3890","It was narrated from Hammad -Ibn Abi Sulaiman- that he was asked about a man who hired a worker in return for food and he said:\n No, not until he tells him (what his wages will be). \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3890 Arabic Hadees: 3890"
"3891","It was narrated from Hammad and Qatadah, concerning a man who said to another man:\n I will lease (something) from you until I reach Makkah for such and such a payment, and if I travel for a month or such and such -something that he named- I will give you such and such in addition.  They did not see anything wrong with that, but they did not like it if he said:  If I travel for more than a month I will deduct such and such from your lease. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3891 Arabic Hadees: 3891"
"3892","It was narrated that Ibn Juraij said:\n I said to 'Ata': 'What if I hire a slave for a year in return for his food, and for another year, in return for such and such?' He said: 'There is nothing wrong with that, and you may stipulate your conditions of hiring even for a few days.' 'How about if I make a deal to hire him when part of the year has passed?' He said: 'Do not hold me to account for what has passed.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3892 Arabic Hadees: 3892"
"3893","It was narrated from Usaid bin Zuhair that he went out to his people, Banu Harithah, and said:\n O Banu Harithah, a calamity has befallen you.  They said:  What is it?  He said:  The Messenger of Allah has forbidden leasing land.  We said:  O Messenger of Allah, what if we lease it in return for some of the grain?  He said,  No.  He said:  We used to lease it in return for straw.  He said:  No.   We used to lease it in return for what is planted on the banks of a stream that is used for irrigation.  He said:  No. Cultivate it (yourself) or give it to your brother. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3893 Arabic Hadees: 3893"
"3894","It was narrated that Usaid bin Zuhair said:\n Rafi' bin Khadij came to us and said: 'The Messenger of Allah has forbidden for you Al-Haql. Al-Haql is the third and the fourth. And Al-Muzabanah. Al-Muzabanah is to buy what is at the top of the date-palm trees in return for a certain number of Wasqs of dried dates.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3894 Arabic Hadees: 3894"
"3895","It was narrated that Usaid bin Zuhair said:\n Rafi' bin Khadij came to us and said: 'The Messenger of Allah has forbidden something that was beneficial for us, but obedience to the Messenger of Allah is better for you. He has forbidden Al-Haql (renting land in return for one-third or one-quarter of the produce) to you, and says: Whoever has land, let him give it (to someone else to cultivate it) or leave it. And he has forbidden Al-Muzabanah. Al-Muzabanah means when a man has a lot of date-palm trees and another man comes and takes it in return for a certain number of Wasqs of dried dates.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3895 Arabic Hadees: 3895"
"3896","It was narrated that Usaid bin Zuhair said:\n Rafi' bin Khadij came to us and I was not sure what he meant. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah has forbidden to you something that used to benefit you, but obedience to the Messenger of Allah is better for you than that which benefits you. The Messenger of Allah has forbidden Al-Haql for you. Al-Haql means share-cropping the land in return for one-third or one-quarter (of the yield). So whoever has land that he does not need, let him give it to his brother (to cultivate it) or let him leave it. And he has forbidden to you Al-Muzabanah. Al-Muzabanah means when a man has a great number of datepalms and says: Take it in return for (a certain number of) Wasqs of dried dates this year.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3896 Arabic Hadees: 3896"
"3897","Usaid bin Rafi' bin Khadij said:\n Rafi' bin Khadij said: 'The Messenger of Allah has forbidden something for you that used to be beneficial for us, but obedience to the Messenger of Allah is more beneficial for us. He said:  Whoever has land let him cultivate it, and if he is unable to do so, let him give it to his brother to cultivate. ' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3897 Arabic Hadees: 3897"
"3898","It was narrated that Mujahid said:\n I took Tawus by the hand and brought him to Ibn Rafi' bin Khadij, and he told him, narrating from his father, that the Messenger of Allah forbade leasing land. Tawus rejected that and said: 'I heard Ibn 'Abbas (say) that he did not see anything wrong with that.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3898 Arabic Hadees: 3898"
"3899","(The previously mentioned chain) from Mujahid who said:\n Rafi' bin Khadij said: 'The Messenger of Allah forbade us to do something that was beneficial for us, (but we respect and obey the command of the Messenger of Allah). He forbade us to lease land in return for some of its produce. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3899 Arabic Hadees: 3899"
"3900","It was narrated that Rafi' bin Khadij said:\n The Prophet passed by the land of a man from among the Ansar who he knew was in need and said: 'Whose is this land?' He said: 'So and so's; he has given it to us in return for rent.' He said: 'Why did he not give it to his brother?'  Rafi' came to the Ansar and said:  The Messenger of Allah has forbidden something for you which was beneficial, but obedience to the command of the Messenger of Allah is more beneficial for you. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3900 Arabic Hadees: 3900"
"3901","It was narrated that Rafi' bin Khadij said:\n The Messenger of Allah forbade Al-Haql (renting land in return for one-third or one-quarter of the produce). \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3901 Arabic Hadees: 3901"
"3902","Rafi' bin Khadij said:\n The Messenger of Allah came out to us and forbade something for us that had been beneficial for us. He said: 'Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or give it to someone else (to cultivate), or leave it.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3902 Arabic Hadees: 3902"
"3903","It was narrated from Tawus and Mujahid, that Rafi' bin Khadij said:\n The Messenger of Allah came out to us and forbade something for us that had been beneficial for us, but the command of Messenger of Allah is better for us. He said: 'Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or leave it or give it (to someone else to cultivate).' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3903 Arabic Hadees: 3903"
"3904","It was narrated that 'Amr bin Dinar said:\n Tawus regarded it disliked renting out land for gold and silver, but he did not see anything wrong with leasing it in return for one-third or one-quarter (of the yield). Mujahid said to him: 'Go to Ibn Rafi' bin Khadij and listen to his Hadith.' He said: 'By Allah, if I knew that the Messenger of Allah had forbidden that I would not have done it. But my Hadith comes from one who is more knowledgeable than him. Ibn 'Abbas (said) that the Messenger of Allah said:  If one of you were to give his land to his brother (to cultivate it), that would be better than taking an agreed portion of the yield. ' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3904 Arabic Hadees: 3904"
"3905","It was narrated from 'Ata' from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah said:\n Whoever has land, let him cultivate it. If he is unable to cultivate it, let him give it to his Muslim brother and not share-crop it with him. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3905 Arabic Hadees: 3905"
"3906","Jabir said:\nThe Messenger of Allah said:  Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or give it to his brother, and not lease it to him. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3906 Arabic Hadees: 3906"
"3907","It was narrated that Jabir said:\n Some people had some extra land which they leased out in return for half of the yield, or one-third, or one-quarter. The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever has land, let him cultivate it, or give it to his brother to cultivate or keep it (without cultivating it).' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3907 Arabic Hadees: 3907"
"3908","It was narrated that Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:\n The Messenger of Allah addressed us and said: 'Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or give it to someone else to cultivate, and let him not rent it out.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3908 Arabic Hadees: 3908"
"3909","It was narrated from Jabir who attributed it to the Prophet:\n That he forbade leasing out land. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3909 Arabic Hadees: 3909"
"3910","It was narrated from Jabir that the Prophet forbade Al-Mukhabarah, Al-Muzabanah and Al-Muhaqalah, and selling fruit until it is fit to eat (ripe enough), except in the case of Al-'Araya. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3910 Arabic Hadees: 3910"
"3911","It was narrated from Jabir that the Prophet forbade Al-Muhaqalah, Al-Muzabanah, Al-Mukhabarah and exceptions when selling, unless they were well-defined. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3911 Arabic Hadees: 3911"
"3912","Jabir narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\n Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or give it to his brother to cultivate, and not lease it to his brother. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3912 Arabic Hadees: 3912"
"3913","It was narrated from Jabir bin 'Abdullah:\n The Prophet forbade Al-Haql and it is Al-Muzabanah. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3913 Arabic Hadees: 3913"
"3914","It was narrated from Jabir bin 'Abdullah that the Prophet forbade Al-Muzabanah and Al-Mukhadarah. He (one of the narrators) said:\n Al-Mukhadarah means selling fruit before it ripens and Al-Mukhabarah means selling grapes in return for a certain number of Sa's. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3914 Arabic Hadees: 3914"
"3915","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\n The Messenger of Allah forbade Al-Muhaqalah and Al-Muzabanah. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3915 Arabic Hadees: 3915"
"3916","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:\n The Messenger of Allah forbade Al-Muhaqalah and Al-Muzabanah. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3916 Arabic Hadees: 3916"
"3917","It was narrated from Rafi' bin Khadij that the Messenger of Allah forbade Al-Muhaqalah and Al-Muzabanah. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3917 Arabic Hadees: 3917"
"3918","It was narrated from 'Uthman bin Murrah who said:\n I asked Al-Qasim about Al-Muzara'ah, so he narrated from Rafi' bin Khadij that the Messenger of Allah forbade Al-Muhaqalah and Al-Muzabanah. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3918 Arabic Hadees: 3918"
"3919","Rafi' bin Khadij said that the Messenger of Allah forbade leasing land. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3919 Arabic Hadees: 3919"
"3920","It was narrated that Abu Ja'far Al-Khatmi - whose name was 'Umair bin Yazid - said:\n My paternal uncle sent me with a slave of his, to Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab to ask him about Al-Muzara'ah. He said: 'Ibn 'Umar did not see anything wrong with it, until he heard the Hadith from Rafi' bin Khadij. Then he met him, and Rafi' said:  The Prophet came to Banu Harithah and saw some crops. He said: 'How good are the crops of Zubair.' They said: 'It is not Zubair's.' He said: 'Is the land not Zubair's?' They said: 'No (it is not his), rather he is leasing it.' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Take your crops and give him what he spent.' So we took our crops, and gave him what he had spent. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3920 Arabic Hadees: 3920"
"3921","It was narrated that Rafi' bin Khadij said:\n The Messenger of Allah forbade Al-Muhaqalah and Al-Muzabanah, and said: 'Only three may cultivate: A man who has land which he cultivates; a man who was given some land and cultivates what he was given; and a man who takes land on lease for gold or silver.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3921 Arabic Hadees: 3921"
"3922","It was narrated that Sa'eed said:\n The Messenger of Allah forbade Al-Muhaqalah.  Sa'eed said:  And he narrated something similar.  And Sufyan Ath-Thawri reported it from Tariq. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3922 Arabic Hadees: 3922"
"3923","It was narrated that Tariq said:\n I heard Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab say: 'Cultivating land is not allowed except in three cases: Land which one owns, land which is given to one, or land which one rents in return for gold and silver.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3923 Arabic Hadees: 3923"
"3924","It was narrated from Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab that the Messenger of Allah forbade Al-Muhaqalah and Al-Muzabanah. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3924 Arabic Hadees: 3924"
"3925","It was narrated that Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas said:\n At the time of the Messenger of Allah landowners used to lease their arable land in return for whatever grew on the banks of the streams for irrigation. They came to the Messenger of Allah and referred a dispute concerning such matters to him, and the Messenger of Allah forbade them to lease land on such terms, and said: 'Lease it for gold or silver.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3925 Arabic Hadees: 3925"
"3926","It was narrated that Rafi' bin Khadij said:\n At the time of the Messenger of Allah we used to lease land on the basis of Al-Muhaqalah, so we would lease it in return for one-third or one-quarter of the yield, or a specified amount of food (produce). One day, a man among my paternal uncles came and said 'The Messenger of Allah has forbidden me to do something that was beneficial for us, but obedience to Allah and His Messenger is more beneficial for us. He has forbidden us to lease land on the basis of Al-Muhaqalah and to lease it in return for one-third or one-quarter of the yield, and for a specified amount of food (produce). And he commanded the landowner to cultivate it (himself) or to give it to someone else to cultivate. He did not like leasing it or anything else.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3926 Arabic Hadees: 3926"
"3927","It was narrated from Ayyub who said:\n Ya'la bin Al-Hakim wrote to me (saying): 'I heard Sulaiman bin Yasar narrating from Rafi' bin Khadij, who said:  We used to lease land on the basis of Al-Muhaqalah, leasing it in return for one-third or one-quarter of the yield, and a specified amount of food (produce). ' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3927 Arabic Hadees: 3927"
"3928","It was narrated that Rafi' bin Khadij said:\n We used to lease land on the basis of Al-Muhaqalah during the time of the Messenger of Allah.  He said that one of his paternal uncles came to them and said:  The Messenger of Allah has forbidden me to do something that was beneficial for us, but obedience to Allah and His Messenger is more beneficial.  We said:  What is that?  He said:  The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever has land, let him cultivate it (himself) or give it to his brother to cultivate, and not lease it in return for one-third or one-quarter of the yield nor a specified amount of food (produce).' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3928 Arabic Hadees: 3928"
"3929","It was narrated that Rafi' bin Khadij said:\n My paternal uncle told me that they used to lease land at the time of the Messenger of Allah in return for what grew on the banks of the streams, and a share of the crop stipulated by the owner of the land. But the Messenger of Allah forbade us that.  I (Hanzalah) said to Rafi':  How about leasing it in return for Dinars and Dirhams?  Rafi' said:  There is nothing wrong with (leasing it) for Dinars and Dirhams. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3929 Arabic Hadees: 3929"
"3930","It was narrated that Hanzalah bin Qais Al-Ansari said:\n I asked Rafi' bin Khadij about leasing land in return for Dinars and silver. He said: 'There is nothing wrong with that. During the time of the Messenger of Allah they used to rent land to one another in return for what grew on the banks of streams and where the springs emerged - some areas of which might give good produce and some might give none at all - and the people did not lease land in any other way. So that was forbidden. But as for leases where the return is known and guaranteed, there is nothing wrong with that.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3930 Arabic Hadees: 3930"
"3931","It was narrated that Hanzalah bin Qais said:\n I asked Rafi' bin Khadij about leasing land. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah forbade leasing land.' I said: 'For gold or silver?' He said: 'No, rather he forbade leasing it in return for what the land produces. As for gold and silver, there is nothing wrong with that.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3931 Arabic Hadees: 3931"
"3932","It was narrated that Hanzalah bin Qais said:\n I asked Rafi' bin Khadij about leasing uncultivated land in return for gold and silver. He said: '(It is) permissible and there is nothing wrong with that. That is the due of the land.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3932 Arabic Hadees: 3932"
"3933","It was narrated that Rafi' bin Khadij said:\n The Messenger of Allah forbade us to lease our land. At that time there was no gold nor silver. A man would lease his land in return for what grew on the banks of streams and where the springs emerged, and in return for something specific. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3933 Arabic Hadees: 3933"
"3934","It was narrated from Az-Zuhri that Salim bin 'Abdullah narrated something similar. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3934 Arabic Hadees: 3934"
"3935","Salim bin Abdullah narrated that Abdullah bin Umar used to lease his land until he heard that Rafi bin Khadij forbade leasing land. Abdullah met him and said:\n O Ibn Khadij, what do you narrate from the Messenger of Allah about leasing land?  Rafi said to Abdullah:  I heard two of my uncles, who had been present at Badr, telling the people in the house, that the Messenger of Allah forbade leasing land.  Abdullah said:  I knew that at the time of the Messenger of Allah land used to be leased.  Then Abdullah was concerned that the Messenger of Allah had decreed something and he had not known about it, so he stopped leasing land. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3935 Arabic Hadees: 3935"
"3936","It was narrated that Az-Zuhri said:\n We heard that Rafi bin Khadij used to narrate that his paternal uncles -whom he said had been present at Badr- (said) that the Messenger of Allah forbade leasing land. \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3936 Arabic Hadees: 3936"
"3937","It was narrated from Shu'aib:\n Az-Zuhri said: 'Ibn Al-Musayyab used to say: 'There is nothing wrong with leasing land in return for gold and silver, and Rafi bin Khadij used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah forbade that.'' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3937 Arabic Hadees: 3937"
"3938","It was narrated from Ibn Shihab that Rafi bin Khadij said:\n The Messenger of Allah forbade leasing land.  Ibn Shihab said:  Rafi was asked after that: 'How did they lease land?' He said: 'In return for a set amount of food (produce), and it was stipulated that we would have whatever grew on the banks of the streams and springs.' \nSunnan e Nisai Hadees: 3938 Arabic Hadees: 3938"
"3939","It was narrated that Anas said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'In this world"
"3940","It was narrated that Anas said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Women and perfume have been made dear to me"
"3941","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""Nothing was dearer to the Messenger of Allah after women than horses"
"3942","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet said:""Whoever has two wives and is inclined to favor one of them over the other"
"3943","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""The Messenger of Allah used to divide his time equally among his wives then he would say: 'O Allah"
"3944","Aishah said:""The wives of the Prophet sent Fatimah"
"3945","It was narrated that 'Aishah mentioned a similar report and said:""The wives of the Prophet sent Zainab and she asked him permission to enter and she entered."" And she said something similar. Ma'mar contradicted the two of them; he reported it from Az-Zuhri"
"3946","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""The wives of the Prophet got together and sent Fatimah to the Prophet. They told her to say: 'Your wives'"" -and he (the narrator) said something to the effect that they are urging you to be equitable with regard to the matter of the daughter of Abu Quhafah. She said: ""So she entered upon the Prophet when he was with 'Aishah under her cover. She said to him: 'Your wives have sent me and they are urging you to be equitable with regard to the matter of the daughter of Abu Quhafah.' The Prophet said to her: 'Do you love me?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then love her.' So she went back to them and told them what he said. They said to her: 'You did not do anything; go back to him.' She said: 'By Allah"
"3947","It was narrated from Abu Musa that the Prophet said:""The superiority of 'Aishah to other women is like the superiority of Tharid to other kinds of food"
"3948","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Prophet said:""The superiority of 'Aishah to other women is like the superiority of Tharid to other kinds of food"
